<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee not to see such cold temps - Somar.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee not to see such cold temps - Somar.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's key coffee areas are now expected to see more seasonal temperatures over the coming weekend due to the entry of a low pressure system in the west of Brazil, local meteorologists Somar said.</p>
<p>Yesterday Somar and other Brazilian forecasters predicted a cold weekend for the country's coffee areas because of a polar air mass which is coming in overland.</p>
<p>Because of the low pressure system however, the Cerrado and southern region of Minas Gerais and north Sao Paulo are now forecast to see cloudy, rainy weather and temperatures are not expected to fall below six degrees Celsius, Somar said in a weather update Thursday.</p>
<p>((--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
